
git init                             Initializes a new Git repository.
ls -a                                Shows all files, including hidden files.
clear                                Clears the terminal screen.
dir                                  Lists files and directories.
ls                                   Lists files and directories.
ls -l                                Shows files with detailed information.
dir /a                               Shows all files, including hidden files, in Windows.
Get-ChildItem -Force                 Shows all files, including hidden files, in PowerShell.
git status                           Shows the current Git repository status.
git add .                            Stages all changed files for commit.
git commit -m "Added sum program"    Saves staged changes as a Git commit.
git log                              Shows the commit history.
git --help                           Shows Git commands and general help.
git commit --help                    Shows detailed help for the git commit command.
git rm one.py                        Removes one.py and stages its deletion.
git restore one.py                   Restores one.py to its last committed state.


git remote add origin https://github.com/USERNAME/REPOSITORY.git
Adds the GitHub repository as a remote named origin.

git remote -v
Shows the fetch and push URLs of the remote repository.

git remote set-url origin https://USERNAME@github.com/USERNAME/REPOSITORY.git
Changes the URL of the existing origin remote.

git remote -v
Verifies the updated remote URL.

clear
Clears the terminal screen.

git push origin master
Pushes the local master branch to the GitHub repository.

